604 - We Know Not the Hour
 / 
Key: Bb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 604
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[F]We know not [Bb]the hour of the Master’s appearing;
[Bb]Yet signs all foretell that the moment is nearing
[F]When He shall return ’tis [F7]the promise most cheering
[Bb]But we know not the hour.

Refrain:
[Bb]He will come, let [F]us watch and be ready;
[F]He will come, hallelujah! hallelujah!
[F]He will come [F7]in the clouds of His Father's
[Eb/Bb]bright glory but we [Bb]know not the hour.

Verse 2:
[F]There's light for [Bb]the wise who are seeking salvation;
[Bb]There's truth in the book of the Lord's revelation;
[F]Each prophecy points to [F7]the great comsummation
[Bb]But we know not the hour.

Verse 3:
[F]We'll watch and [Bb]we'll pray, with our lamps trimmed and burning;
[Bb]We'll work and we'll wait till the Master's returning;
[F]We'll sing and rejoice, every [F7]omen discerning
[Bb]But we know not the hour.
